    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "The quick way (about 1 minute)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ol",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Open "
            },
            {
              "text": "Compress to 20 KB",
              "href": "/tools/compress-image-to-20kb"
            },
            {
              "text": " on your phone’s browser."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Tap "
            },
            {
              "text": "Take photo",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " to use the camera, or "
            },
            {
              "text": "Choose from gallery",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " to pick a saved image."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The target is already 20 KB, and the page tells you the file will be 18–20 KB. Compression starts by itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "SahiSize finds the highest quality that still fits under 20 KB, making the picture smaller in pixels if it needs to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Check the size shown (for example “18.7 KB”) and the ticks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Tap "
            },
            {
              "text": "Download",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". The file is saved with your photo’s name plus "
            },
            {
              "text": "-20kb.jpg",
              "code": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", for example "
            },
            {
              "text": "IMG_1234-20kb.jpg",
              "code": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "This page does not crop. If you need to cut away background or fit a fixed shape, use your exam page or "
        },
        {
          "text": "Signature Resize",
          "href": "/tools/signature-resize"
        },
        {
          "text": ", which both have a crop box."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Everything happens inside your browser. The photo is not uploaded to any server, so it works even on a slow connection once the page has loaded."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "If your exam also checks pixels (like IBPS 200 × 230), use the exam page instead — for example "
        },
        {
          "text": "IBPS PO",
          "href": "/exam/ibps-po"
        },
        {
          "text": " — so both pixels and KB are set together."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Why most apps make it blurry"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Most “compress” apps only lower JPG quality. A 3000 × 4000 px photo at very low quality might reach 20 KB, but it looks blocky and smeared."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "The better method:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ol",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Crop first.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Throw away background you do not need (on your exam page or in the signature tool)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Reduce pixels.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " A passport photo does not need 12 million pixels. 200 × 230 or 276 × 354 px is plenty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Then adjust quality.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " With fewer pixels, the photo hits 20 KB at a good quality."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "SahiSize reduces pixels before quality automatically; the exam pages also crop first. More on why pixels and KB are different in "
        },
        {
          "text": "KB vs pixels — simple explanation",
          "href": "/guides/photo-size-kb-vs-pixels"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Tips for a sharp 20 KB file"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ul",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Start from the original.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Do not use a photo you received on WhatsApp — it is already compressed and loses more detail each time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Plain background.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " A plain light wall compresses far better than a patterned curtain. Detail costs KB."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Good light.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Dark, grainy photos have noise, and noise needs more KB. Daylight from a window is best."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Signatures compress easily.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " A clean black-on-white signature usually reaches 10–20 KB at high quality. Use "
            },
            {
              "text": "Signature Resize",
              "href": "/tools/signature-resize"
            },
            {
              "text": ", which also whitens the paper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Stay just under the top.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Some portals count 1 KB as 1,000 bytes, so a 19.9 KB file (20,378 bytes) can fail a 20 KB limit. SahiSize keeps a safety margin: a 20 KB target lands at about 18.5–19 KB, which passes either way."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "The minimum-KB trap"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "If your target is a range like 20–50 KB, going too low is also an error. Signatures and plain photos often come out "
        },
        {
          "text": "too small",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " — 12 KB, 15 KB — even at full quality."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "SahiSize’s exam pages and signature tool handle this: for range targets they raise quality, then slightly increases pixels within the allowed limits, and only if still short add invisible padding. You get a file inside the range without visible change."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "For other targets, there are ready pages: "
        },
        {
          "text": "10 KB",
          "href": "/tools/compress-image-to-10kb"
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "30 KB",
          "href": "/tools/compress-image-to-30kb"
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "50 KB",
          "href": "/tools/compress-image-to-50kb"
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "100 KB",
          "href": "/tools/compress-image-to-100kb"
        },
        {
          "text": ". For any custom number, use "
        },
        {
          "text": "Compress Image",
          "href": "/tools/compress-image"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "On iPhone"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "iPhone photos are often saved as "
        },
        {
          "text": "HEIC",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ", which many portals do not accept. SahiSize reads HEIC and outputs a normal JPG, so you can compress and convert in one step. In Safari, the downloaded file goes to the Files app → Downloads."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "On Android"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Chrome saves downloads to the Downloads folder. When the exam portal asks you to choose a file, tap "
        },
        {
          "text": "Browse",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " or "
        },
        {
          "text": "Files",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ", then "
        },
        {
          "text": "Downloads",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ". Pick the file that ends in "
        },
        {
          "text": "-20kb.jpg",
          "code": true
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "FAQ"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "How do I check the size of a photo on my phone?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "On Android, open the photo in Files and tap the info (i) icon. On iPhone, open it in the Files app and long-press → Get Info. SahiSize also shows the KB before you download."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "My photo is 20 KB on my phone, but the portal says “image size too large”. Why?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Your phone may round. The file might be 20.4 KB, or the portal may count 1 KB as 1,000 bytes. Stay a little under: up to 19.5 KB (19,968 bytes) passes both ways of counting. SahiSize’s 20 KB page lands at 18–20 KB, usually about 19 KB."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Can I reduce photo size to 20 KB without losing quality?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Some loss is unavoidable at 20 KB, but if you crop first and reduce pixels to the size the exam wants, the photo still looks clear at normal viewing size."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Will compressing change my face or remove the background?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "No. SahiSize only crops, resizes and compresses. It does not edit your face or change the background."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Is this the official IBPS or SSC tool?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "No. SahiSize is independent and not linked to any exam body. Always check the latest official notice. If your photo was rejected, see "
        },
        {
          "text": "why your photo got rejected",
          "href": "/guides/photo-rejected-how-to-fix"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
